<title>FRANCE: Renault workers head for new occupation in France.</title>
<headline>Renault workers head for new occupation in France.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian employees of French carmaker Renault on Thursday left a new car depot near the northern city of Lille they had been occupying to head for another assembly plant near the Belgian border, union sources said.</p>
<p>They plan another protest at the Maubeuge Construction Automobile plant, which employs 2,500 workers and works on a new Renault model, the X76.</p>
<p>The workers, from Renault's Vilvoorde plant in Belgium, had been in the plant near Lille since March 20, when they impounded about 1,800 new cars as &quot;hostages&quot; to try to stop Renault from closing Vilvoorde and shedding nearly 2,800 jobs.</p>
<p>Renault has said the decision to close the plant is irrevocable.</p>
</text>
